2106		There exists a function
2107		$\delta_S(\eps,m,d,q) = a(md)^a(\eps^b + q^{-b} + 2^{-bmd})$, for some
2108		universal constants $a > 1$ and $0 < b < 1$, such that the following
2109		holds. For
2110		$\hilb \in \{\hilb_{\mathsf{A}}, \hilb_{\mathsf{B}}\}$ there
2111		exists a projective measurement $\{\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}\}$ acting on
2112		$\hilb \ot (\C^q)^{\ot M}$, with outcomes consisting of pairs
2113		$(g_X, g_Z)$ of polynomials, each in $\mathrm{ideg}_{d,m}(\F_q)$, such
2114		that for $W \in \{X, Z\}$, on average over uniformly random
2115		$u \in \F_q^m$,
2116		\begin{align}
2117			\big(\hat{S}_{[\mathrm{eval}_u(\cdot_W) = a]}
2118			\big)_{\mathsf{A}\mathsf{A}'}
2119			&\simeq_{\delta_S}
2120			\big(\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Point},W),u}_{a}
2121			\big)_{\mathsf{B}\mathsf{A}''}\,,
2122			\label{eq:qld-s-point-con-alice} \\
2123			\big(\hat{S}_{[\mathrm{eval}_u(\cdot_W) = a]}
2124			\big)_{\mathsf{B}\mathsf{B}'}
2125			&\simeq_{\delta_S}
2126			\big(\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Point},W),u}_{a}
2127			\big)_{\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}''}\,,
2128			\label{eq:qld-s-point-con-bob}
2129		\end{align}
